  "semantics": "Each input is a complete manifest byte string given to the viewer-side validator. 'expected' is the 0.3 result (first rule and stage, actual eth_getCode requests). 'expected02' records the behaviour of the draft 0.2 tooling where it differs or where the fixture is a precedence control; it documents why the fixture discriminates and is checked against m1-draft-0.2/tools/rlp_strict.py. Hex inputs are literal. 'construction' inputs are built by tools/rlp_strict.nest(inner, depth), which wraps inner in depth canonical list headers; headHex/tailHex/length are literal checks on the constructed bytes.",
  "depthFacts": {
    "maxNestedEmptyListsWithin65536Bytes": 21916,
    "derivation": "s(1)=1 (0xc0); s(d+1)=s(d)+header(s(d)) with header 1 byte below 56, 2 bytes below 256, 3 bytes below 65536, 4 bytes below 2^24. s(56)=56, s(156)=256, s(156+k)=256+3k, so s(21916)=65536 and s(21917)=65536+4=65540.",
    "codexProbeInputBytes": 3391,
    "codexProbeNote": "coordination/review-001/independent-probes.json used a 3391-byte input; 3391 = s(1201)."
  },
